IMPORT prelude

-- Brothers of St. Gabriel Ordinance 1950 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Titular Superior of the Brothers of St. Gabriel in
-- Singapore" is and who stands in for the Titular Superior during a vacancy (s 2), what the Ordinance empowers it to do (s 2(2), s 3),
-- how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 4), what a Gazette notification proves (s 5), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves
-- alone (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSGO1950.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 6. The Ordinance is dated 2 March 1950. Section numbers follow the body (s 1 short title
-- to s 6 saving); the arrangement at the top of the deposit is garbled by the PDF extraction but carries the same six headings.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0229 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance is six sections long, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside the Congregation it matters mainly when
-- buying, leasing or lending on the security of the Corporation's property, or suing it about that property (s 3), and in checking
-- that the Corporation's deed was executed by the right person (ss 2(3), 4, 5).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 4(1) refers (whether
-- a power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); how a Titular Superior or Brother Procurator is
-- appointed, and what "formal assumption of office" consists of, about which the Ordinance says nothing; the Corporation's internal
-- governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Brothers of St. Gabriel Ordinance 1950 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 2(3) -- who is the Corporation, and who stands in during a vacancy`

-- s 2(1): "The Reverend Brother Vincent, the Titular Superior of the Congregation of the Brothers of Christian Instruction of
-- St. Gabriel, in the Colony of Singapore, and his successors in office, shall be a body corporate", named "The Titular Superior of
-- the Brothers of St. Gabriel in Singapore", with perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 2(3): "successors in office" is "deemed to include the Brother Procurator from the time when the office ... becomes vacant by the
-- resignation or death of the holder for the time being until the formal assumption of office by his successor."
--
-- The deeming names two causes of vacancy only: resignation and death. A vacancy arising any other way (the text does not mention
-- one; removal or transfer are examples supplied here, not by the text) does not, on the words, make the Brother Procurator a
-- successor in office. The deeming ends at the successor's "formal assumption of office", not at his appointment.
DECLARE Vacancy IS ONE OF
    `the office is filled`
    `vacant by resignation`
    `vacant by death`
    `vacant for some other reason`

GIVEN `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacant` IF
    CONSIDER `the vacancy`
    WHEN `the office is filled` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy, `the successor has formally assumed office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Brother Procurator is deemed a successor in office` IF
        (NOT `the successor has formally assumed office`)
    AND CONSIDER `the vacancy`
        WHEN `vacant by resignation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `vacant by death` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5 -- what a notice in the Gazette proves`

-- s 5: "A notification in the Gazette of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Titular Superior ... or of the
-- Brother Procurator shall be conclusive evidence that such person was duly authorised to exercise the said office in the Colony of
-- Singapore."
--
-- The Gazette proves authorisation conclusively for either office; without it, authorisation is a matter of other evidence, which
-- the Ordinance does not regulate (so the encoding returns FALSE for "conclusively proved", not "not authorised").
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `Titular Superior`
    `Brother Procurator`
    `some other office in the Congregation`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office, `the appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
        `the appointment is notified in the Gazette`
    AND CONSIDER `the office`
        WHEN `some other office in the Congregation` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(2) and 3 -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed or altered or made anew as to the Corporation seems fit."
-- s 3(1): the Corporation "may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, exchange, surrender, yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable or
-- immovable property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
-- s 3(2): "The Corporation may sue and be sued in respect of such property in any of the Courts of the Colony of Singapore."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". The capacity to sue and be sued is given "in respect of
-- such property"; the Ordinance grants no other power (whether the general law supplies one is outside the text and not encoded).
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `exchange property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `be sued in respect of its property`
    `sue on a matter not about its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `exchange property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `sue in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `be sued in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 4(1): instruments requiring the seal "shall be sealed with the seal of the Corporation in the presence of the person who is the
-- Titular Superior for the time being ..., or when the office is vacant, in the presence of the Brother Procurator or of the Attorney
-- of any one of them duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act
-- 1886, and shall also be signed by the said Titular Superior for the time being ... or by the Brother Procurator as the case may be
-- or the Attorney of any one of them so authorised as aforesaid."
-- s 4(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed and that the
-- same is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- Readings encoded (inferences from the wording, not stated):
--   * The Brother Procurator qualifies only "when the office is vacant" (and, for signing, "as the case may be"); while the office is
--     filled, only the Titular Superior or an attorney qualifies.
--   * The Titular Superior qualifies only while the office is filled ("for the time being").
--   * "the Attorney of any one of them" is read as an attorney of either officer, qualifying whether or not the office is vacant,
--     provided the power of attorney was deposited. An attorney whose power was not deposited never qualifies.
--   * s 4(1) speaks of the office being "vacant" without the "resignation or death" limit of s 2(3). The encoding follows s 4 here, so
--     the Brother Procurator may execute in any vacancy, though s 2(3) deems him a successor only in two kinds of vacancy. The two
--     sections are not reconciled by the text.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Titular Superior`
    `the Brother Procurator`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `another Brother`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer, `the office is vacant now` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may act for the Corporation under section 4` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Titular Superior` THEN NOT `the office is vacant now`
    WHEN `the Brother Procurator` THEN `the office is vacant now`
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 4 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may act for the Corporation under section 4` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`) (`the office is vacant` `the vacancy`)
    AND `may act for the Corporation under section 4` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) (`the office is vacant` `the vacancy`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may act for the Corporation under section 4` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) (`the office is vacant` `the vacancy`)

§§ `6 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Ordinance contained shall affect the rights of the Government, all bodies politic and corporate, and all
-- others, except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from and under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
